  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="be6ca65d-dd07-584e-82cf-280eefc5e806" activityNameId="5b11f2d4-9b09-5c42-966e-bfd3200685ca" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Copper, primary, at refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Copper, primary, at refinery
The product "copper, primary, at refinery" is used as pure metal or as alloying element in various technical applications.;
UUID: 2e8910df-fbe3-308a-b2e0-4c6afbbe7fcc
The module includes the pre-treatment of the ore, the reduction and the refining copper to cathode copper, including the country-specific share in hydrometalurgically won copper (SX-EW)
Location: This module is valid for the whole corresponding region. Some agents used like lime or sodium cyanide originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe.
Technology: The ore is pre-treated,  reduced and refined according to the country specific mix of process alternatives: reverberatory furnace 23.7%; flash smelting furnaces 60.7%; other 6.2%.; SX-EW 9.4%. An overall abatement for sulphur dioxide of 45.4% was estimated.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 9.5 million tonnes in Cu in 1994
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2e8910df-fbe3-308a-b2e0-4c6afbbe7fcc.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="79ab44d1-ff60-537f-a4a8-d0fd401f4529" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
